  "history": "Founded in New York in 2000 by Josh Wolfe, Peter H\u00e9bert and Robert Paull, Lux Capital began as a nanotechnology research house as much as a venture firm: its 2001 site described funding \"start-up capital, or the first outside funds a company raises\" in information technology and nanotechnology, and its first portfolio page (2005) listed seven companies, among them Nanosys, Molecular Imprints, Cambrios and the firm's own spin-out Lux Research. That habit of building as well as backing runs through the book \u2014 the firm's pages record Genocea as \"founded by Lux in 2006 as a spin-out of Harvard Medical School\", Kala Pharmaceuticals as a Johns Hopkins spin-out it founded, and Everspin as a spin-out it ideated and helped lead out of Freescale. The modern firm is a deep-tech and defence investor writing first checks: Anduril (2017), Applied Intuition (2017), Zoox (2015), Planet (2013), Relativity Space (2016), Saildrone (2016), Varda (2021) and Impulse Space (2022) on the hardware side; Recursion, Eikon, EvolutionaryScale and a large biology book on the science side; and Hugging Face (Series A, 2019), Runway, Together, Sakana AI, Cognition and Physical Intelligence in AI. Exits include Auris Health (Johnson & Johnson, 2019), CTRL-labs (Facebook, 2019), MosaicML (Databricks, 2023), Nervana (Intel, 2016), Luxtera (Cisco, 2019), Kurion (Veolia, 2016) and a cohort that listed by SPAC in 2020-21 (Desktop Metal, Matterport, Aeva, Rigetti, Evolv, Shapeways, Latch, Science 37). Lux Ventures IX closed at $1.5B in January 2026, the firm's largest fund.",
  "investment_concept": "Backs scientists and engineers building companies at the edges of the possible -- defence and aerospace, robotics and advanced manufacturing, semiconductors and photonics, biology and health, and the computing infrastructure underneath them. Lux writes first institutional checks and frequently co-founds or incubates companies out of university and corporate research, then follows into later rounds through dedicated opportunity and co-invest vehicles.",
